{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F8QPjM7eHD1E3uoAnwyBzh","type":"tool_result","content":"31:## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n93:## Recognition cues -> first move\n121:## Day by day\n122:**Days 1-6** (base64, ROT13, hex, 8-bit binary, decimal, zero-padded octal): one layer each, solved in seconds-minutes.\n128:**Days 7-9** (URL `%xx`, decimal HTML entities, quoted `\"\\u00XX\"` JSON string): one layer each, CORRECT in 18-53 s.\n135:**Days 10-13** (base32; unpadded base64url; reversed sentence; Atbash): one layer each, CORRECT in 5-73 s.\n142:**Days 14-19** (Caesar +7; ROT47; Morse over hex; Bacon a/b 5-groups over hex; rail fence 3/offset 0; hex of UTF-16LE\n152:**Day 20: Big Entrance** (\"Same bar. This time the big one goes first.\" -- hex of UTF-16BE with BOM).\n163:## GM answer conventions learned\n169:## Pitfalls that cost time\n- **Text encoding / byte order under hex (D19-D20)** -- values seen: D19 single/TT one lowercase hex string starting\n  `fffe` (UTF-16LE BOM) then `4e00 6900 ...` (char + `00`), 436 B single; D20 single/TT starting `feff` (UTF-16BE BOM)\n  then `004e 0069 ...` (`00` + char), 440 B single. Mastery line 19 = `fffe` + LE (`fffe2d006a0075006e006900` = `-juni`),\n  line 20 = `feff` + BE (`feff007000650072002d00330035` = `per-35`): EACH fragment carries its OWN BOM, and the two\n  byte orders sit side by side in one blob, so the order must come from each line's BOM, never from the day. Parse\n  rule (D19 solver `_hex_utf16`): `fromhex`; BOM `fffe`/`feff` -> `decode('utf-16')` (BOM consumed, endianness from it);\n  no BOM but `00` at every odd/even byte -> `utf-16-le`/`-be`; accept only printable output. Check `fffe0000`/`0000feff`\n  (UTF-32) and `efbbbf` (UTF-8 BOM) BEFORE UTF-16 -- UTF-32LE also \"decodes\" as UTF-16LE with NUL chars. The plain hex\n  branch must not claim it: a latin-1 fallback gives `ÿþN\\x00i\\x00...` (looks like text with NULs, no slug). The D19\n  solver's BOM-aware `_hex_utf16` and lib `decode_chunk` took D20 (single, TT, all 98 line-20 fragments) UNCHANGED:\n  writing the BOM-honouring generic rule on day N covered day N+1's knob turn. Next knobs on this axis: no BOM (NUL\n  position), UTF-32 (`fffe0000`/`0000feff`), UTF-8 BOM, another outer layer (b64/b32/binary) -- all prebuilt.\n- **Line wrapper** -- `NN<TAB>fragment` numbering; fragments split mid-word and join verbatim in number order.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"864226a6-bf71-42ae-8ce9-0226dbd6fa77","uuid":"d9dd2792-1841-4a89-b43f-683a291edfe3","timestamp":"2026-10-20T13:18:16.782Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"31:## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n93:## Recognition cues -> first move\n121:## Day by day\n122:**Days 1-6** (base64, ROT13, hex, 8-bit binary, decimal, zero-padded octal): one layer each, solved in seconds-minutes.\n128:**Days 7-9** (URL `%xx`, decimal HTML entities, quoted `\"\\u00XX\"` JSON string): one layer each, CORRECT in 18-53 s.\n135:**Days 10-13** (base32; unpadded base64url; reversed sentence; Atbash): one layer each, CORRECT in 5-73 s.\n142:**Days 14-19** (Caesar +7; ROT47; Morse over hex; Bacon a/b 5-groups over hex; rail fence 3/offset 0; hex of UTF-16LE\n152:**Day 20: Big Entrance** (\"Same bar. This time the big one goes first.\" -- hex of UTF-16BE with BOM).\n163:## GM answer conventions learned\n169:## Pitfalls that cost time\n- **Text encoding / byte order under hex (D19-D20)** -- values seen: D19 single/TT one lowercase hex string starting\n  `fffe` (UTF-16LE BOM) then `4e00 6900 ...` (char + `00`), 436 B single; D20 single/TT starting `feff` (UTF-16BE BOM)\n  then `004e 0069 ...` (`00` + char), 440 B single. Mastery line 19 = `fffe` + LE (`fffe2d006a0075006e006900` = `-juni`),\n  line 20 = `feff` + BE (`feff007000650072002d00330035` = `per-35`): EACH fragment carrie