64 with `.` `/` and digits first | `str.translate` to the std alphabet then std decoder; shuffled alphabet: solve from crib | med: knob on D1/D10 |\n| 136 | SCSU / BOCU-1 / UTF-EBCDIC compressed or exotic Unicode forms | gap (gap scsu-bocu-compressed) | yes | hex mostly ASCII bytes plus `0x0E`-`0x1F` tag bytes (SCSU) | small stdlib SCSU decoder; BOCU-1 table | low |\n| 137 | \"same codec, one knob turned\" sweep over every seen day's codec (bit/byte order, case, separators, padding, alphabet, polarity, shift k, rails/offset, BOM) | gap (gap knob-sweep-prior-codecs) | yes | prompt starts \"Same ...\" / \"Again\" / \"This time ...\"; blob LOOKS like a seen day but no strict branch yields a slug | enumerate each `DAYS` codec's parameter space inside the slug gate | high: D20 established the pattern |\n\"\"\"\nanchor=s.index(\"| 127 |\")\nend=s.index(\"\\n\",anchor)+1\ns=s[:end]+rows+s[end:]\n# recognition cues\nrep(\"\"\" hex x4 starting fffe/feff, 00 every 2nd byte = UTF-16 (D19: .decode('utf-16')); fffe0000 -> UTF-32;\"\"\",\n\"\"\" hex x4 starting fffe (D19 LE 4e00) / feff (D20 BE 004e), 00 every 2nd byte = UTF-16: .decode('utf-16') reads EITHER BOM;\n   fffe0000/0000feff -> UTF-32; NULs at 2 of 4 non-adjacent -> middle-endian; d8xx dcxx -> surrogates, then NFKC;\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\" tail); D19 line 19 has its OWN BOM.\"\"\",\"\"\" tail); D19/D20 lines 19/20 each have their OWN BOM (LE and BE in one blob).\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"Title pun -> key: a cipher name + a number/word in the prompt = the key (D18 \"Three rails\"); verify on the crib.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Title pun -> key: a cipher name + a number/word in the prompt = the key (D18 \"Three rails\"); verify on the crib.\n\"Same ...\"/\"This time ...\" prompt (D20) = yesterday's codec with ONE knob turned (byte/bit order, alphabet, width).\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\" [0-7] 3-digit ................... octal (D6);   [0-9] 32-126 tokens -> decimal (D5); 1-26 dashed -> A1Z26\"\"\",\n\"\"\" [0-7] 3-digit ................... octal (D6);   [0-9] 32-126 tokens -> decimal (D5); 1-26 dashed -> A1Z26\n ONE long digit run, no spaces .... whole text as a big integer (to_bytes big/little); 4-10 digit tokens -> u16/u32 words\"\"\")\n# gaps json\na=s.index(\"```json\",s.index(\"## Readiness gaps\"))+len(\"```json\\n\")\nb=s.index(\"```\",a)\ngaps=json.loads(s[a:b])\nbuilt={\"utf-family-sweep\",\"base64-utf16le\",\"endian-word-swap\",\"wide-int-charcodes\",\"hexdump-formats\",\"binary-lsb-first\",\"raw-wide-artifact\",\"nibble-swap-hex\",\"leb128-varint\",\"gsm7-septet-packing\"}\nkeep=[g for g in gaps if g[\"id\"] not in built]\nfor g in keep:\n    if g[\"id\"]==\"byte-family-mastery-cost\":\n        g[\"detail\"]=(\"D20 Mastery 98 x 20 solved in 18.6 s with a BYTE-IDENTICAL D19 solver (D19 93 x 19 = 2.5 s, D17 83 x 17 = 1.35 s): \"\n          \"a 7x jump for +1 line, a third of the harness's 60 s kill budget. Per-line decode_chunk of a line-20 fragment is instant, so profile answer() \"\n          \"per set (joint free search? fallbacks? host load?) BEFORE adding tomorrow's branch; keep return-early, run new byte-level sniffers only on bytes a \"\n          \"strict branch already produced, and time hctf solver-test on the real Mastery case.\")\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"knob-sweep-prior-codecs\",\"concept\":\"'same codec, one knob turned': parameter sweep over every seen day's codec\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D20 = D19's codec with byte order flipped ('Same bar. This time the big one ...'). Build warmups_codecs.knob_sweep(t): for each DAYS codec enumerate its knobs -- hex case/separators/0x/byte order per 2/4/8, binary bit order + width 7/8/16, octal/decimal width and radix, base32/64 alphabet+padding variants, Morse dot/dash swap + separators, Bacon polarity/width, rot/Caesar k and direction, rail rails x offset, UTF BOM/order/width, reversal at char/byte/nibble/word level -- and return the first crib/slug-gated read. Also register as a free fallback for unclaimed Mastery lines. Cost cap: < 0.2 s per blob, cheap knobs first. Fixtures: one knob turned on each of D1-D20.\"},\n {\"id\":\"middle-endian-pdp\",\"concept\":\"middle-endian / PDP-11 byte order (2143, 3412) for 32-bit words, UTF-32 or u32 char codes\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Third act of the bar joke: little (D19), big (D20), middle next. Hex whose 4-byte words read neither as utf-32-le nor -be: e.g. 'N' as UTF-32 in PDP order = '0000 4e00' -> bytes '00 00 4e 00' vs BE '00 00 00 4e'. Also UTF-16 code units in 32-bit middle-endian words. Decode: try all 24 permutations of each 4-byte word (and 2-byte swaps inside), then utf-32-be/utf-16-be, crib-gated; BOM 'feff' permuted ('fffe0000' variants) as a cue. Fixtures: PDP 2143/3412 UTF-32 hex, with/without BOM, + 6-8 char Mastery fragments.\"},\n {\"id\":\"bignum-integer-text\",\"concept\":\"whole message as ONE big integer (int.from_bytes big/little) written in decimal / octal / base36 / base62 / binary\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"'Big' pun / number family: RSA long_to_bytes style. Cue: one unbroken run of digits (~2.41 decimal digits per plaintext char, ~265 for the sentence), no separators; or a single [0-9a-z] base36 token. Decode n=int(t,base); n.to_bytes((n.bit_length()+7)//8,'big') and the 'little' variant; also of UTF-16 bytes (then BOM sniff). Crib-gated. Mastery: each fragment its own integer (6-8 chars -> ~17 digits). lib.decode must not claim a long digit run as decimal char codes (no separators = not tokens).\"},\n {\"id\":\"swapped-codeunit-escapes\",\"concept\":\"D9-style code-unit escapes with byte order swapped: \\\\u4e00\\\\u6900, &#x4e00;, U+4E00, %u4E00, 0x4e00\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Knob turn on an older codec in the D19-D20 direction. Cue: escapes that json.loads/html.unescape to CJK U+4E00-U+7Exx only, every low byte 00. Decode: swap bytes of each 16-bit value ((v&255)<<8|v>>8), then chr. Also UTF-16 surrogates written as escape pairs. Hook after the strict escape branches of decode_chunk behind the slug gate. Fixtures for \\\\u, &#x, U+, %u forms, LE-swapped and normal.\"},\n {\"id\":\"wide-binary-codeunits\",\"concept\":\"16/32-bit binary groups of UTF-16/UTF-32 code units, BE or LE (halves swapped)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D4 binary + D19/D20 width/order knob. Cue: [01]{16} (or {32}) groups split by spaces, the high or low 8 bits all zero. Decode int(g,2).to_bytes(2,'big'/'little') -> utf-16 (BOM group '1111111011111111' = feff if present). Also no-space 16-bit streams (len%16==0). Fixtures: u16be/u16le binary, with/without BOM group, u32.\"},\n {\"id\":\"astral-utf16-surrogates\",\"concept\":\"non-BMP / non-ASCII text under a byte layer: math-alphanumeric letters as UTF-16 surrogate pairs, CESU-8, Modified UTF-8 (c0 80), overlong UTF-8\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Cue: UTF-16 hex with d835 dcxx pairs (Mathematical Bold 𝐍 = U+1D40D), or UTF-8 hex with ed a0..ed bf (CESU surrogates) or c0/c1 lead bytes (overlong). Decode: utf-16 with surrogatepass, CESU via surrogate-pair join, overlong via lenient manual UTF-8 decoder; then NFKC to ASCII; lowercase the slug. Fixtures under hex and base64.\"},\n {\"id\":\"byte-add-offset\",\"concept\":\"bytewise add/subtract k mod 256 (Caesar on bytes) under hex / base64 / binary\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Distinct from XOR (prebuilt). Cue: decoded bytes non-printable but (c-p) mod 256 constant over the crib 'Nice work...'. Decode k=(c0-0x4e)%256 then verify all crib bytes; both directions. Also 16-bit add on UTF-16 code units. Fixtures k in {1,7,13,47,128} under hex/b64.\"},\n {\"id\":\"byte-rotate-bits\",\"concept\":\"per-byte bit rotation ROL/ROR 1-7 and per-byte bit reversal under hex/base64\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Cue: hex bytes none printable, popcount per byte equal to ASCII's (rotation preserves it). Try 7 rotations (ROL 4 = nibble swap, already prebuilt) crib-gated; bit reversal = binary-lsb-first at byte level. lib.binary has _rolb/_ror8 to reuse. Fixtures ROL1..7 hex + b64.\"},\n {\"id\":\"base-n-alt-alphabets\",\"concept\":\"alternate base-N alphabets: Crockford base32, z-base-32, Geohash-32, crypt/bcrypt base64 (./0-9A-Za-z), shuffled/keyed base64 alphabet\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Knob turn on D1/D10/D11. Cue: base32-looking text with lowercase z-base set (ybndrfg8ejkmcpqxot1uwisza345h769) or Crockford (0-9A-Z minus I L O U, '-' separators allowed); base64 with '.' '/' and digits at low indices. Decode via str.translate to the RFC alphabet then std decoder; keyed alphabet: recover from the crib (87 known chars give most of the mapping). base32hex already prebuilt. Fixtures each alphabet + padding variants.\"},\n {\"id\":\"scsu-bocu-compressed\",\"concept\":\"SCSU / BOCU-1 / UTF-EBCDIC exotic Unicode forms\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Low odds. SCSU for ASCII text is mostly identity bytes plus window tags 0x0E-0x1F; a ~60-line stdlib decoder. BOCU-1 and UTF-EBCDIC via tables. Crib-gated; only if cheap.\"},\n]\nout=new[:5]+[g for g in keep if g[\"priority\"]==1]+new[5:9]+[g for g in keep if g[\"priority\"]==2]+new[9:]+[g for g in keep if g[\"priority\"]==3]\nassert len({g[\"id\"] for g in out})==len(out)\nbody=\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in out)+\"\\n]\\n\"\ns=s[:a]+body+s[b:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\ns=open('/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/warmups.md').read()\na=s.index(\"```json\",s.index(\"## Readiness gaps\"))+8;b=s.index(\"```\",a)\ng=json.loads(s[a:b]);st=json.load(open('/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/.run/prebuild-state.json'))\npend=[x[\"id\"] for x in g if x[\"action\"]==\"prebuild\" and not (st.get(\"warmups:\"+x[\"id\"],{}).get(\"ok\") or st.get(\"warmups:\"+x[\"id\"],{}).get(\"attempts\",0)>=2)]\nprint(len(g),pend,len(pend))\nprint(set(x.keys()) for x in g[:1